ISSUE TITLE: JEV-Based Intelligent Model Selection & Routing
ISSUE DESCRIPTION:
Hi Team,

It would be great to add JEV-style intelligent model selection and routing to FreeLLMAPI.

Instead of relying only on static routing rules such as round-robin, priority, or model availability, FreeLLMAPI could use JEV to analyze the incoming task and dynamically select the most suitable model based on factors such as:

- Task type and complexity
- Model capabilities and quality
- Token efficiency and context requirements
- Cost/free-tier availability
- Current model availability and limits

Potential workflow:

- User sends a request to FreeLLMAPI.
- JEV analyzes the task and determines the required capabilities.
- JEV selects the most appropriate model/provider, considering both output quality and token efficiency.
- FreeLLMAPI routes the request to that model.
- Optionally, the result can be evaluated and retried with another model if needed.

This could make FreeLLMAPI a more intelligent model-agnostic routing layer, particularly useful when users have multiple models with different strengths, context limits, token costs, and free-tier constraints.

Ideally, JEV could be offered as an optional routing strategy alongside the existing routing methods.

-Sam

